Anyway, to answer the questions: Why? Because it's fun and because
people like to be #1. How? Well you simply take advantage of the
various "features" the game to get a level 30 player, with 18/** 25 18
25 25 25 stats, 1000 hp, AC -128, a blessed +20 Excalibur, a million
gold pieces, and a bag of holding with 10000 dilithium crystals in it.

These scores are high, although I'm sure others out there can do
better. I think it's quite possible to break one billion points in
nethack 3.0.10, although I don't know of anyone so far who has done so
(yet), although My "Angel" game was over 1/4 of the way there. I
notice that if ever one were to pass 2^31 points (i.e. 2 billion 100
million) the score will turn over and go negative. Doing this would
involve doubling the work involved in getting a billion point game, or
be about eight 250M games linked back to back. I assume that this
would be the ultimate in nethack 3.0 - turning over the high score
list, or else stopping and ascending at exactly 2,147,483,647 points
for a technically unbeatable high score.

